  "term": "Psychosocial Intervention",
  "definition": "A psychosocial intervention is a psychological or social intervention delivered by a wide range of providers, including mental health professionals, other health professionals, religious leaders, lay or peer providers, paraprofessionals, caregivers, and automated formats such as internet-, audio-, or video-delivered programs. More than one type of provider may be involved together.",
